From: Ludovic Zammit <luzammi@akamai.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] security_event: gate Fingerbank lookups and accounting_events_history KEYS scan on is_api_key_configured

info_for_security_event_engine is called per auth via security_event_trigger
(provisioner check in role.pm:391, hostname/connection-type change checks in
api.pm:1277/:1302). It always writes per-MAC fingerbank cache entries
(mac_vendor_id_from_mac_*, dhcp_*_id_*) AND always runs
pf::accounting_events_history->latest_mac_history, which issues a blocking
KEYS accounting_events_history:data-* against redis_cache (Redis is
single-threaded; KEYS is O(N) and serializes all clients).

When Fingerbank is intentionally disabled (no API key in fingerbank.conf),
pf::fingerbank::process already short-circuits (fingerbank.pm:93). This patch
mirrors that same gate here so the supporting lookups skip too.

Behavior change: with no API key configured, device_id, dhcp_*_id,
mac_vendor_id, and last_accounting_events in the security_event info struct
are undef/[]. Security_events that match those attributes will stop firing
when Fingerbank is off -- consistent with process() already returning early.

Measured impact on an 8 vCPU all-in-one box during MAC auth load tests:
redis_cache CPU dropped from ~48% to ~5%, eliminated 80k+ blocking KEYS
calls per 60s test, and sustained Access-Accept rate climbed from ~67/sec
to ~150-170/sec.

Apply from /usr/local/pf/:

    patch -p1 < 0001-security_event-gate-fingerbank-when-api-key-not-configured.patch

Then rebuild containers that ship lib/ (e.g. pfperl-api) and restart any
host-side Perl workers (e.g. packetfence-pfqueue-backend) so they reload the
module.

---
 lib/pf/security_event.pm | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/pf/security_event.pm b/lib/pf/security_event.pm
--- a/lib/pf/security_event.pm
+++ b/lib/pf/security_event.pm
@@ -519,6 +519,8 @@ sub info_for_security_event_engine {

     my $cache = pf::CHI->new( namespace => 'fingerbank' );

+    my $fb_enabled = fingerbank::Config::is_api_key_configured();
+
     $type = lc($type);

     my $devices = [];
@@ -526,7 +528,7 @@ sub info_for_security_event_engine {
     if($type eq "device"){
         $device_id = $tid;
     }
-    else {
+    elsif ($fb_enabled) {
         my ($device_result, $device) = fingerbank::Model::Device->find([{name => $node_info->{device_type}}]);
         if(is_success($device_result)){
             $device_id = $device->id
@@ -540,20 +542,27 @@ sub info_for_security_event_engine {
         dhcp6_enterprise => "fingerbank::Model::DHCP6_Enterprise",
     };
     my $results = {};
-    foreach my $attr (keys %$attr_map){
-        my $model = $attr_map->{$attr};
-        my $query = {value => $node_info->{$attr}};
-        $results->{$attr} = $cache->compute_with_undef("$model\_id_".encode_json($query), sub {
-            my ($status, $result) = $model->find([$query]);
-            return is_success($status) ? $result->id : undef;
+    if ($fb_enabled) {
+        foreach my $attr (keys %$attr_map){
+            my $model = $attr_map->{$attr};
+            my $query = {value => $node_info->{$attr}};
+            $results->{$attr} = $cache->compute_with_undef("$model\_id_".encode_json($query), sub {
+                my ($status, $result) = $model->find([$query]);
+                return is_success($status) ? $result->id : undef;
+            });
+        }
+    }
+    my $mac_vendor_id;
+    if ($fb_enabled) {
+        ($mac_vendor_id) = $cache->compute_with_undef("mac_vendor_id_from_mac_$mac", sub {
+            my $mac_vendor = pf::fingerbank::mac_vendor_from_mac($mac);
+            return $mac_vendor ? $mac_vendor->id : undef;
         });
     }
-    my ($mac_vendor_id) = $cache->compute_with_undef("mac_vendor_id_from_mac_$mac", sub {
-        my $mac_vendor = pf::fingerbank::mac_vendor_from_mac($mac);
-        return $mac_vendor ? $mac_vendor->id : undef;
-    });

-    my $accounting_history = pf::accounting_events_history->new->latest_mac_history($mac);
+    my $accounting_history = $fb_enabled
+        ? pf::accounting_events_history->new->latest_mac_history($mac)
+        : [];


     my $last_ip = pf::ip4log::mac2ip($mac) || 0;
